>search attic
Armed with a flashlight, it's a lot easier to sort through all this junk and detritus... you wonder who it belongs to, since Rob, the guy renting this place, probably doesn't have a lot of use for an artillery manual or a sky blue wig... what's this?

There's a bottle of wine hidden here. Only it's not normal wine.

>drink wine
Sure, the wine tastes like it should've been drunk about five centuries ago, and honestly it really does taste like pumpkin juice, or what pumpkin juice would taste like if there were such a thing. But it's got character. And more importantly, it makes you feel different and pleasant. The stuff is obviously potent, but somehow it doesn't feel like you're going to get trashed.

It makes you feel like life is being nicely chilled before being served to you. It also makes you want to dance.

>down

Second Floor Landing
Christmas lights twist around the railing leading down. There are enough of them that the the walls of the stairway are the hue of fruit salad, the kind with tiny oranges, not the other kind, the kind with apple slices. Ugh. That awful shade of brown they turn once they're exposed to air for too long.

Stairs go up and down, and there's a hallway to the west.

>down

